ODW8110 [*] Missing `return` (`super` is used) in method copy
  --> missing_return.py:20:9
   |
18 |     # The call is the last statement, so the `return` can go in front of it even though
19 |     # other statements run first.
20 |     def copy(self, default=None):
   |         ^^^^
21 |         self.check_access("read")
22 |         super(MyModel, self).copy(default)
   |
help: Return the `super()` call
   |
21 |         self.check_access("read")
   -         super(MyModel, self).copy(default)
22 +         return super(MyModel, self).copy(default)
23 |
   |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

ODW8110 Missing `return` (`super` is used) in method default_get
  --> missing_return.py:26:9
   |
24 |     # Storing the result and doing nothing with it: only the author knows whether the
25 |     # variable, `super()`'s value, or something else should be returned.
26 |     def default_get(self, fields):
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^
27 |         res = super().default_get(fields)
28 |         res["name"] = "x"
